WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
- We need to start with a big congrats.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.060
I don't know if anybody,
everybody knows, but last month,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.280
you said that you'd been
undergoing cancer treatment

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.080
for a year, which I didn't know about,

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.212
so I don't know that
many people knew about.

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:09.045
- You were not supposed

00:00:09.045 --> 00:00:09.878
to know about it.
- Yeah, I was like,

00:00:09.878 --> 00:00:10.711
I don't think many people knew about.

00:00:10.711 --> 00:00:12.153
- I kept it quiet.
- You did.

00:00:12.153 --> 00:00:13.950
- Yes.
- And you got the news

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.360
that you're now cancer free, right?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.193
- I am.

00:00:16.193 --> 00:00:19.110
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.460
- [Terry] Thank you.
- That's a hard thing

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.559
to keep quiet.

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:23.100
- I...

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:23.970
Listen.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.290
- [Kelly] Just physically
while you're working.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.123
- Yeah, it is.

00:00:26.123 --> 00:00:27.570
It was hard.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.290
The thing was, I didn't
wanna say anything.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.850
I don't want pity and I
don't have a publicist

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.130
that you released it and everybody says,

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.190
oh my God, Kelly's, oh, you
know, I didn't want that.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.330
That happens.
- Yeah.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:43.440
- I just wanted to keep it quiet.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.000
My family knew.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.520
And then as you can tell,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.250
I'm a little subconscious
about my appearance

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.320
but that's from the treatments

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.630
and people were saying,
what's wrong with me?

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.070
What's wrong with me?

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.020
And so finally I thank Fox

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.720
for allowing me the time to say -

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:01.553
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:03.700
- In November I was diagnosed
with bladder cancer.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.000
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And I went on treatments

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.040
at Baylor, I mean Baylor,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.040
Yale Medical Center up
in New Haven, Connecticut

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.490
for six weeks.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:19.470
Then I came back and was diagnosed
weeks later, cancer free.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.210
But I still do follow up treatments

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.070
which I still have to go back up for that.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.663
- Which are hard on your body.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.700
- You have no idea.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.050
I had no idea.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.150
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- 'Cause it was,

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.350
it's bladder cancer.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.440
And then in March I'm getting ready to go

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.800
to Hawaii and I'm all excited
I get a vacation after,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.940
well over two years and I was
having trouble with my neck

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:46.380
and I go in, my wife says,
we need to get that checked.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.753
And then they found a tumor here.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.470
So that's Merkel cell cancer.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.303
- Oh my God.
- That's a form

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:55.320
of skin cancer.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.190
It's relatively rare,
had it not been for this

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.216
then we wouldn't have found that.

00:02:00.216 --> 00:02:01.049
- [Kelly] Yeah they didn't catch it.

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:04.320
- So they cut all that out
and now my face is a little,

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.190
I'm self-conscious.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.320
My wife says, you look fine.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.310
But -
- Yeah, I gotta be honest

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.273
with you, it just isn't out, yeah.

00:02:09.273 --> 00:02:10.106
- If I had -
- [Kelly] I didn't know.

00:02:10.106 --> 00:02:11.389
- But you know what Kelly,

00:02:11.389 --> 00:02:14.790
it's like I'm so
self-conscious of my face.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.340
One good thing about it though,

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.920
I don't have to shave 'cause
I have no hair over here.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.330
So it was, it's been a long battle.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.170
And then I went back to MD Anderson

00:02:27.408 --> 00:02:30.210
and got, I'm cancer free here.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.351
So as we do this interview.
- [Kelly] Jeez.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.003
- What a blessing though, yeah.

